Pattern Structure

The system applies the Composite Pattern using:

ProductComponent as the common interface
Product as the leaf object
Category as the composite object

This structure allows the system to treat individual products and groups of products uniformly.

Class Responsibilities
ProductComponent

Defines common operations for all products and categories.

Product

Represents a single product in the system.

Category

Represents a group that may contain:

Products
Subcategories

It supports recursive operations for displaying products and calculating total prices.

Pattern Behavior

The client interacts only with the ProductComponent interface.
This reduces dependency on concrete classes and supports loose coupling.

The Category object recursively manages child components, which enables flexible hierarchical structures.
